{"event_type":"review","id":"bed53ca800490ab353c1b04bae2fa9710b50e996b4719cfe545bb703eaa5328c","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T17:37:37Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cb1a13e50a0a72541c5cd6f3131b0ea4b532634523a34c841310b41a79779f6f","sha256":"cb1a13e50a0a72541c5cd6f3131b0ea4b532634523a34c841310b41a79779f6f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4122d9d5944915a2f6f990ab84e0bcdc07112e9ecf655f767497d4aae1616f96","sha256":"4122d9d5944915a2f6f990ab84e0bcdc07112e9ecf655f767497d4aae1616f96"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/486c833d57fb78e539ac7644d4e042229cc218162c75214b20eda4bfc23e5c30","sha256":"486c833d57fb78e539ac7644d4e042229cc218162c75214b20eda4bfc23e5c30"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dba8d59ef85e0c891b634163ac6356a2a0c63904729afec9814a1b5ae0d480d9","sha256":"dba8d59ef85e0c891b634163ac6356a2a0c63904729afec9814a1b5ae0d480d9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b90404c27fd1afcc31b8ee0bfc164ded86b3ba395eddf29eeac780b938e1030f","sha256":"b90404c27fd1afcc31b8ee0bfc164ded86b3ba395eddf29eeac780b938e1030f"}],"attempt_id":"aa1a8b9d6c847bd470bdcc2c32dfc50a6a390f77cefe96864e32b8adcda16f18:0:1","base":"cfdefdb6553f6249903cd32609f2ac5b5b194d27","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"fe2151023c1ac2aa3f745300ad0cd14210f205c1","body":"**Type `markersOf` with `TamperConfig`.**\n\n`hackDetector` accepts `HackDetectorInput.tamper?: TamperConfig`, but `markersOf` passes `Record<string, unknown>`. The `unknown` values are incompatible with `TamperConfig` fields, and `test/` is included in `tsconfig.json`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  async function markersOf(diff: string, tamper?: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<string[]> {\n+  async function markersOf(\n+    diff: string,\n+    tamper?: NonNullable<Parameters<typeof hackDetector>[0]['tamper']>,\n+  ): Promise<string[]> {\n```\n\n</details>","id":"0d6d9e67fbf481eb8ac37fbf3b3379caa55f6770ea94265cdc4455fe23ed6cf2","intervals":[],"path":"test/ops/gates/hackDetector.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Type `markersOf` with `TamperConfig`."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b96117a3968aaa6d79834e9e13bd7dff64a6239d","body":"**Keep the root error when rollback fails.**\n\nIn `src/kernel/journal.ts:512-517`, a rejection from `markReleased()` or `handle?.close()` replaces the acquisition error. `markReleased` can reject from `writeDurable`, `stat`, `readLockRecord`, `rename`, or `syncDir`. A failed `markReleased` leaves the unreleased record canonical. Same-host contenders then refuse through `assertReclaimable` (`journal.ts:591-608`) while this process is alive.\n\n`acquirePlanLock` has the same masking at `journal.ts:354`. A rejection from `acquired.release()` replaces the fence or guard-release error. The guard-release catch at `journal.ts:337-340` already keeps the root cause.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   } catch (error) {\n     try {\n       if (listening) await closeServer(server);\n       // Publication and owner setup are one rollback scope; markReleased\n       // only ever replaces a record that is provably ours.\n-      await markReleased();\n+      await markReleased().catch(() => undefined);\n     } finally {\n-      await handle?.close();\n+      await handle?.close().catch(() => undefined);\n     }\n     throw error;\n   }\n```\n\n```diff\n   } catch (error) {\n-    await acquired.release();\n+    await acquired.release().catch(() => undefined);\n     throw error;\n   }\n```\n</details>","id":"36a348c72d2d8e2a1676e4c3e5d2aff01acfb4d28ad517235a2b096384b614db","intervals":[],"path":"src/kernel/journal.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Keep the root error when rollback fails."}],"head":"b34fcce37beca2b0b5dad843ab644d48a3ffceee","head_tree":"a044c2d307ae73d8952cea17b0d4c6811610cdec","input_scope":[{"blob":"b96117a3968aaa6d79834e9e13bd7dff64a6239d","intervals":[[8,10],[24,46],[65,773],[786,787],[813,819],[821,821],[844,847],[850,850],[853,860],[867,867],[870,885],[921,1141],[1175,1175],[1179,1202],[1214,1233],[1267,1267],[1319,1341]],"path":"src/kernel/journal.ts"},{"blob":"e933615a2f2672408c73921bf705a5ac96c24ff1","intervals":[[26,26],[28,36],[42,42],[45,45],[47,47],[52,76],[80,85],[88,105],[128,201],[215,220],[222,229],[231,237],[239,261],[263,277],[279,328],[331,343],[345,353],[355,365],[389,393],[395,454],[456,466],[468,509],[511,602],[622,1172],[1177,1203]],"path":"src/kernel/schema.ts"},{"blob":"fe2151023c1ac2aa3f745300ad0cd14210f205c1","intervals":[[1,1],[30,33],[45,45],[59,59],[73,73],[182,182],[184,185],[196,196],[198,199],[324,324],[377,392],[399,399],[402,403],[407,407],[409,409],[425,428],[517,517],[521,521],[526,528],[590,675],[685,685],[688,688],[690,690],[746,1134]],"path":"test/ops/gates/hackDetector.test.ts"}],"job_id":"aa1a8b9d6c847bd470bdcc2c32dfc50a6a390f77cefe96864e32b8adcda16f18:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"efdd989a9156e5a533a16400dcbf6bfd2770c595","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/kernel/journal.ts"},"merge":"6a842e1e1bf6ffde44dd9d8f561a01d702b4bb34","method":"pre-merge","pre":"5170bdc4c98ac6712fb87c0109c31445488629f1","source_path":"src/kernel/journal.ts"},"blob":"b96117a3968aaa6d79834e9e13bd7dff64a6239d","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/kernel/journal.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"e83a8200811d37f3c95e2ea3b9ab9b5d04bccf09","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/kernel/schema.ts"},"merge":"6a842e1e1bf6ffde44dd9d8f561a01d702b4bb34","method":"pre-merge","pre":"5170bdc4c98ac6712fb87c0109c31445488629f1","source_path":"src/kernel/schema.ts"},"blob":"e933615a2f2672408